  "mach:accessModel": "open",
  "mach:governance": "academic",
  "mach:maturity": "production",
  "mach:category": "specs",
  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Mature OWL ontology for classifying health IT software, published as CC0 Linked Open Data with a live SPARQL endpoint — one of the few genuinely machine-actionable health software vocabularies. Useful as a reference taxonomy for labelling and classifying catalog entries, and as a complementary resource to MACH: HITO provides ontological structure, MACH provides editorial curation and recommendations. Marked Assess rather than Adopt because its primary audience is semantic web and ontology engineers rather than software practitioners, and community adoption remains modest (11 stars). The CC0 licence and SPARQL endpoint make it straightforward to integrate.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-13",
